messages:
liz: Heads-up — noticed the API reference for POST /v1/generate has an inconsistent request example. It shows "inputs" as an array but our runtime expects an object with a "prompt" field for the latest model. Also the JS snippet still uses the old client.generate({ prompt }) shape. Can someone take this?

omar: I can take a quick pass. do we want to show both old and new shapes (migration) or just update to the current canonical example? :thinking_face:

liz: Prefer both — short migration callout at top + canonical example. Callout should say: "If you previously used an array `inputs: [...]` or `client.generate({prompt: ...})`, see migration note below." Keep examples minimal.

chen: dropping a suggested canonical request here:```json
POST /v1/generate
{
  "model": "redwood/fast-7b",
  "input": {
    "prompt": "Summarize the following text:",
    "max_new_tokens": 150
  }
}
```This mirrors the runtime change to a single `input` object + `max_new_tokens`.

omar: thanks. one small thing — the API ref currently documents `max_tokens` in some places. we should standardize on `max_new_tokens` and add a one-line note about the token naming change for older clients. i'll open a PR.

liz: great. include a tiny JS SDK snippet that matches current SDK surface:```js
// npm @redwood/inference v3+
const { Redwood } = require('@redwood/inference');
const client = new Redwood();
await client.responses.create({
  model: 'redwood/fast-7b',
  input: { prompt: 'Summarize...', max_new_tokens: 150 }
});
```and mark the old snippet under an "Upgrade note" section.

sarah: also add links to the SDK changelog & the migration guide we merged last quarter (docs/migrations/2025-prompt-shape). otherwise folks will be confused. i can review the PR once open. :thumbsup:

omar: PR opened at https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/412 — includes: updated example, migration note, and adjusted cURL + python snippets. pinging @sarah @chen for reviews. deploy-bot: queued render job.

deploy-bot: Render started for PR #412 — docs site preview: https://deploy-preview-redwood-docs.netlify.app/preview/412

chen: quick nit — in cURL example we should explicitly set Content-Type: application/json; some users copy/paste without it. i'll add that to the PR.

liz: perfect. once approved can we backport a short paragraph to the API changelog (2026-02) so customers searching by token param names find it?

omar: yup will add changelog note in the PR description. aiming to merge today after reviews. thanks all!

sarah: LGTM once the header and changelog are added. thanks for moving quickly.

omar: merged and deployed. closing thread.
